skip_lines":["cogs","gp","rd","sga","oox","op","oth"],"checks":{"quarters_tied":24,"notes":["revenue: Jackson adopted LDTI (the new long-duration insurance accounting) in 2023 and restated 2022. The 2023 10-Qs carry Q1 to Q3 of 2022 on the new basis, but the only filed Q4 2022 quarter is the old-basis one in the 2022 10-K (revenue -381, net income -710). Those Q4 figures are left out so Q4 2022 is the restated full year less the restated nine months, which matches the recast 8-K of May 10 2023 (pre-tax -1,543, tax -385, net income -1,150, diluted EPS -13.74). Revenue reads -2,029 against -2,014 in that 8-K because the 2025 10-K moved 15 million out of 2022 revenue.","FY2022Q4: EPS -13.74 set in the company map (Recast 8-K of May 10 2023 (2022 restated for LDTI): Q4 2022 net loss attributable to Jackson of 1,150 million, diluted EPS -13.74). The only filed Q4 2022 EPS (-8.48, 2022 10-K) is on the old pre-LDTI basis; the page reads Q4 2022 on the restated basis.","FY2022Q4: diluted shares 86.807m set in the company map (Q4 2023 release of Feb 21 2024, prior-year column: weighted average diluted shares outstanding 86,807,053 for Q4 2022 (restated for LDTI))","shares: Full year less nine months gives 135.6 million because the restated year mixes a loss quarter with profitable ones. The release count is used, as for every other quarter. In loss quarters Jackson's GAAP EPS divides by basic shares (about 83.7 million here), so EPS times this count runs about 43 million below net income.","1 quarters read from the latest filings only so lines share a basis (FY2022Q4 to FY2022Q4)","reporting template financial: not shown cogs, gp, rd, sga, oox, op, oth","FY2022Q4: eps x sh off ni by -43","seg: FY2020Q3 to FY2026Q3, 25 quarters"]}}